G6a-13 sampled sync progress, reporting and classification, 2026-09-08
Base commit: ff2e6fe (G6a-9), branch dev.
Working-tree base: G6a-10/11/12 uncommitted standalone/multi-task/registration work.
Environment: local Darwin; Linux amd64 cross-compilation only.

Scope:
- Explicitly enabled, bounded, separate AUTH/INFO replication source probes.
- Coherent cached local capture/apply/GC confirmation/resource observation.
- Local snapshot is taken before source INFO; newer local progress cannot be
  paired into an older source sample while that request is in flight.
- Exact decimal-string positions/byte gaps in JSON; no secrets/endpoints/paths.
- Optional task heartbeat progress, SQLite persistence, derived runtime views.
- Worker/Server share conservative lineage/freshness/error classification.
- Not execution authorization, an atomic barrier, cold health, or eviction proof.
- No automatic warming/eviction/write rejection, failover or task assignment.
- No real Redis/Kvrocks progress integration, deployment, Linux systemd run,
  long stability run, throughput/latency result, trend alarm or notification.

Coverage:
- INFO role, replid and offset parsing; duplicates/malformed/oversized replies,
  negative/overflow offsets, all-zero history, non-master sources and credentials.
- Read-only AUTH/INFO transcript, no PSYNC/data writes/cold requests; connection
  timeout/cancellation/close, cache-before-probe ordering and local source binding.
- Distinguish applied from persistent GC confirmation, unknown GC from zero lag.
- Same-history ordered comparison only; omit gaps on stale/unknown/error/uncertain
  or mismatching samples; sample_aligned is explicitly not current cold health.
- Large offsets above 2^53 and near int64 max round-trip without API precision loss.
- Sample age is not refreshed by lifecycle updates or repeated heartbeats.
- Server elapsed receive time, transport allowance, offline/conflict overrides.
- 8-task reports remain within the existing 16KiB limit; old reports still valid.
- Read-only status/metrics/check-config never trigger source probes.
- Three independent in-flight samplers cancel and join alongside task shutdown.
- Concurrent immutable cache snapshots, fixed metrics labels and omitted stale gaps.
- Source/store/HTTP fixtures are controlled local tests, not real data replication.

Review/test-driven corrections:
- Compare identical retries using JSON wire values, not time.Time internal
  monotonic/location state that is intentionally absent after SQLite decoding.
- Capture Server receive time before waiting on the store mutex, so queuing does
  not make old samples fresh; add conservative 3s reporting transport allowance.
- Use 45s sample freshness to cover bounded sampling + heartbeat cadences, while
  still aging cached samples independently from newly received heartbeats.
- Do not publish fresh local progress after a non-pressure resource observation
  failure; preserve the previous sample and its original age.

